<figure class="force-balance reckoning-visual">
  <header>
    <p>Force balance on half a chain</p>
    <h3>The slope records how much chain hangs below</h3>
  </header>

  <div class="diagram-shell">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 860 390" role="img" aria-labelledby="force-title force-desc">
      <title id="force-title">Forces acting on the right half of a hanging chain</title>
      <desc id="force-desc">
        A magenta chain segment rises from its lowest point to a cut point on the right. At the cut,
        a diagonal tension arrow has horizontal component H and vertical component w times s. The
        vertical component balances the weight of the chain segment, whose arc length is s.
      </desc>

      <g aria-hidden="true">
        <path class="waterline" d="M75 330H795" />
        <path class="chain-halo" d="M120 315C250 313 360 285 455 220S632 97 735 78" />
        <path class="chain" d="M120 315C250 313 360 285 455 220S632 97 735 78" />
        <circle class="point" cx="120" cy="315" r="7" />
        <circle class="cut" cx="555" cy="151" r="9" />
        <path class="cut-mark" d="m543 139 24 24m-23 0 23-24" />

        <path class="arrow tension" d="M555 151L701 63m-20 4 20-4-8 19" />
        <path class="arrow horizontal" d="M555 151H701m-18-10 18 10-18 10" />
        <path class="arrow weight" d="M555 151V292m-10-18 10 18 10-18" />

        <text class="label tension-label" x="674" y="48">tension T</text>
        <text class="label horizontal-label" x="710" y="156">H</text>
        <text class="label weight-label" x="571" y="283">ws</text>
        <text class="label" x="295" y="296">arc length s</text>
        <text class="small-label" x="83" y="349">lowest point</text>
        <text class="small-label" x="518" y="128">imaginary cut</text>

        <path class="angle" d="M604 151A49 49 0 0 0 597 126" />
        <text class="angle-label" x="611" y="132">θ</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <figcaption>
    <strong>What to notice:</strong> the horizontal force <em>H</em> stays constant. The vertical
    force must equal the weight <em>ws</em> of the chain between the lowest point and the cut. As
    arc length <em>s</em> grows, the tangent angle <em>θ</em> grows too.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

